<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sahure</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2487–2475 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/25th-century-bce">25th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sahure was the second king of the 5th Dynasty of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. He built his pyramid at Abusir, whose causeway and temple reliefs show seagoing ships returning from an expedition, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo-stone">Palermo Stone</a> records the first known Egyptian expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-of-punt">Punt</a> in his reign, which brought back <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myrrh">myrrh</a>, electrum and other goods. He also sent expeditions to the turquoise mines of Sinai.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sahure.jpg" alt="Sahure" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Sahure_and_a_Nome_God_MET_DP-1691-04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
